      0.5500   0.869     14.1561     0.3976     1.6956
  -> the surface fit barely moves while the core error swings widely.
     That is the whole identifiability problem in one table: k is an INPUT.

  Entropic-term sensitivity (Forgez et al. 2010, dU/dT = -0.5 mV/K at 50% SOC):
    off (headline)         R_eff 14.3040 mOhm  surf 0.4637 K  CORE 0.8895 K
    on, -0.50 mV/K         R_eff 14.1452 mOhm  surf 0.4652 K  CORE 0.8927 K
  NOTE: T_s is used in the reversible term, not T_c -- using the core
        temperature there would be a leak.  A fixed dU/dT at 50% SOC is an
        approximation; the SOC window here is only 11% wide, which limits
        the error that introduces.
